  "finalText": "All 14 weekend tickets are triaged. Twelve are still open, with a severity, a deadline and an assignee. Two were closed as non-requests and two were merged away. I made no pages and opened no incidents.\n\n**Closed as not service requests**\n- T-2010 is a marketing email.\n- T-2014 is an out-of-office auto-reply.\n\n**Merged as duplicates**\n- T-2005 went into T-2004, the earlier CRM search report. It is now department impact.\n- T-2012 went into T-2003, the earlier Payments build report. It is now department impact.\n- Neither ticket in either pair had a deadline, so each survivor got the new sev2 deadline of 12:10Z today.\n\n**Triaged tickets**\n\n| Ticket | Severity | Due (UTC) | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2003 payments builds | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-101 Dana Whitfield |\n| T-2004 CRM search | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2006 payslip tax code | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2007 phishing | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-601 Noor Haddad (security-oncall) |\n| T-2011 overtime import | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2013 Lisbon VPN | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2001 Berlin VPN | sev3 | Mon 17:00 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2002 CRM filter | sev4 | Thu 17:00 | E-203 Amara Osei |\n| T-2008 VPN client update | sev4 | Thu 17:00 | E-302 Marcus Feld |\n| T-2009 build logs | sev4 | Thu 17:00 | E-102 Ravi Menon |\n\n**Where the rules decided the result**\n- **T-2006:** a single-user payroll ticket is normally sev3. KB-55 (the payroll close amendment, 20–31 March) makes it sev2.\n- **T-2007:** the requester typed a password into a fake page, so it is a security incident. I set it sev2 and assigned it to the security-oncall engineer, even though it came in on VPN.\n- **T-2001:** it was created while the desk was closed, so its 480 business minutes start at 09:00 today.\n- **Sev4 tickets:** their 1440 business minutes run from 09:00 Monday. The 25 March holiday doesn't count, so they fall due Thursday 17:00.\n- **Sev2 tickets:** these run on the clock, so they are due 240 minutes after triage, at 12:10.\n- **Leave cover:** E-301 is on leave today, so the network-secondary on-call, E-303, took T-2001 and T-2013. E-202 is on leave Thursday, so the business-apps-secondary on-call, E-203, took T-2002.\n\nI didn't escalate any ticket, because triage doesn't call for it.",
